proVBFH-cs: VBF Higgs production at (N)NLO, fully differential, with a line-by-line
Catani-Seymour projection to Born. The inclusive part (structure functions),
the analysis and the VBFNLO matrix elements are those of ../proVBFH; this
package has no POWHEG-BOX machinery. Design: docs/DESIGN.md. Summary of the
study that led to this code: ../notes/2026-10-cs-summary/README.md (the full
logbooks and study tools are in the git tag cs-study-2026-10).

BUILD
  Build ../proVBFH first (./configure, make): proVBFH-cs takes the tool paths
  from ../proVBFH/Makefile.inc (hoppet >= 2.0.0, LHAPDF, FastJet) and its
  inclusive-part sources from ../proVBFH/src.
    make                      builds proVBFH-cs (analysis of proVBFH)
    make ANALYSIS=p1506       builds proVBFH-cs-p1506 (analysis/p1506_analysis.f,
                              the 1506.02660 histograms, incl. 3- and 4-jet rates)
    make ANALYSIS=hxswg136    builds proVBFH-cs-hxswg136 (HXSWG 13.6 TeV analysis)
    make check                builds and runs tests/test_kinematics, test_smallx
                              and test_four; fails if one of them fails
    make clean

HOW TO RUN
  Run in a directory that has powheg.input and vbfnlo.input (as proVBFH).
  example/ has the cards of the 1506.02660 set-up (13 TeV, PDF 261000, VBF cuts,
  dynamic scale, runningscales 1) with every cs_ flag written out at its
  default. For example, from a copy of example/:
    cp -r example /my/run && cd /my/run && /path/to/proVBFH-cs-p1506
  One run does the inclusive part and then the exclusive part, and adds the
  histograms. For production runs (many seeds on a Slurm cluster) see
  production/slurm: make_jobs.sh (one directory per seed from a card of
  production/<setup>), run_array.sh (Slurm array task), combine_and_plot.sh
  (combine the seeds, plot against the old proVBFH).

  ncall1, itmx1: VEGAS grid pass; ncall2, itmx2: main pass. They are used as given
  for the exclusive part. The inclusive part (7 dimensions) uses the mapped
  numbers: n <= 1e4 -> n, 1e4 < n <= 1e7 -> n/10, n > 1e7 -> n/100.
  iseed sets the seed; the random numbers of the exclusive part restart from it.
  readingrid 1 reads the grids of a previous run with the same seed instead
  of the grid pass (grids<seed>.dat for the inclusive and grids-excl<seed>.dat
  for the exclusive part; both are written by a normal run).

FLAGS (powheg.input; absent = default)
  cs_order 3        QCD order: 1 LO (inclusive part only), 2 NLO, 3 NNLO
                    (qcd_order is not used)
  cs_scales 3       scale points computed on the fly: 1 central only; 3 adds
                    (1/2,1/2) and (2,2) (W2, W3); 7 adds (1/2,1), (1,1/2),
                    (2,1), (1,2). Needs runningscales 1 unless cs_scales 1
  cs_npow 0         sampling power of 1-xp and z (0: logarithmic)
  cs_cutoff 1d-5    invariant cutoff on 1-xp, z, 1-z of the line radiations
  cs_hardfrac 0.3   fraction of first line radiations in the hard channel (small
                    xp, z ~ 1/2), for the high-pT tails
  cs_hardfrac2 0.7  the same for the second emission of the four-parton generator
  cs_hard2mode 1    1: the second-emission hard channel only behind the hard
                    first step; 0: after every first step
  cs_smallx 0.3     fraction of Born phase-space points in the small-x channels
                    (0: off)
  cs_smallx_x0 0.03 x limit of the small-x channels
  cs_4qint 1        identical-quark interference in the four-quark reals of
                    the (2,0) and (0,2) parts (H + 4 quarks): normal x flipped
                    diagrams when the gluon-split pair has the flavour of the
                    radiating line (NC) or of one end of its W line (CC);
                    0: off, as before 2026-10-13 (validation/v4_4qint);
                    2: the interference alone, to measure its effect: the
                    exclusive part (pwg-EXCL-W<k>.top) is then only the
                    interference and its counterevents (needs cs_order 3;
                    the inclusive part is run as usual and must be ignored;
                    setreal warns once per entry without interference
                    ("rflav ... flav+tag") at initialisation)

OUTPUTS (in the run directory)
  pwg-W<k>.top      all histograms, total (inclusive + exclusive), scale point k
                    (W1 central; with the analysis weights of cs_scales)
  pwg-LO-W<k>.top   inclusive part alone;  pwg-EXCL-W<k>.top  exclusive part alone
  xsct-<lo|nlo|nnlo>.dat   cross section with the cuts of the analysis, per scale point
  grids.dat, grids-excl.dat (plus .top) VEGAS grids; run.log is the standard output
  At cs_order 1 only the inclusive part is run (pwg-LO-W<k>.top and pwg-W<k>.top).

VALIDATION (validation/)
  v1_regression.sh  the combined run reproduces the earlier two-job set-up
                    (inclusive and exclusive part run separately), bin by bin
                    (needs that older binary, see the script)
  v2_submit.sh, v2_check.py, v2_sizing.txt
                    physics check of the default card at NLO and NNLO against
                    production/results/final-2026-10-07 (Slurm array)
  v3_cleanup.sh     the clean-up changed nothing: default example card (and the
                    p1506 binary), cs_order 1, 2, 3, against binaries built
                    before the clean-up, every histogram bin and the xsct file to
                    1e-12 relative (v3_compare.py)
  v4_4qint/         cs_4qint: the four-quark real matrix element of the program
                    against an independent Dirac-matrix reference (ref.f90),
                    pointwise for all 1640 four-quark entries, cs_4qint 1, 0
                    and 2, and the scaling of the interference in the single-
                    unresolved limits (run_v4.sh); e2e_4qint.sh: cs_4qint 2 =
                    cs_4qint 1 - cs_4qint 0 bin by bin at equal points;
                    effect.py, pilot-4qint-W<k>.top: the effect on p1506 (20
                    jobs of cs_4qint 2). Results in RESULT.txt
  make check        unit tests (tests/)
